3,"text":226},{"id":232,"depth":367,"text":233},{"id":243,"depth":367,"text":244,"children":393},[394],{"id":247,"depth":373,"text":248},{"id":264,"depth":367,"text":265,"children":396},[397,398,399],{"id":268,"depth":373,"text":269},{"id":285,"depth":373,"text":286},{"id":298,"depth":373,"text":299},{"id":311,"depth":367,"text":312,"children":401},[402,403],{"id":315,"depth":373,"text":316},{"id":342,"depth":373,"text":343},"Looking back at the best pictures from my travel adventures in 2023","md","\u002Fimages\u002F2023-visual-journey\u002Fcover-image.png",{},true,"\u002Fblog\u002F2023-travels-visual-journey","2024-01-01",false,{"description":413,"title":5},"Travel photos from 2023 across Nepal, Croatia, France, Germany, Monaco, Hungary, the Netherlands and Spain, from Plitvice Lakes to Montserrat.","blog\u002F2023-travels-visual-journey",[416,417,418],"personal","travel","photography","hiking-photography",null,"kULVBfQfkko-VuV65ObfGLO_AAxBx_b_6HBonM5Q2as",[423,434,442,453,462,474,483,489,496,505],{"title":424,"description":425,"tags":426,"postDate":432,"path":433,"url":420,"topic":427},"Why I let AI agents change my OS only through Nix","AI agents make it trivial to change your operating system and hard to remember what they changed. Here's why I manage NixOS and macOS from one Nix config in Git.",[427,428,429,430,431],"nixos","nix","nix-darwin","ai","developer productivity","2026-11-26","\u002Fblog\u002Fconfiguring-my-os-with-nix-in-the-age-of-ai",{"title":435,"description":436,"tags":437,"postDate":440,"path":441,"url":420,"topic":419},"A browser tool that puts every carousel photo on the same white mat, like a gallery print","Instagram can keep each photo's original aspect ratio in a carousel, but I prefer a white canvas with even borders. I built a page that pads every image onto one shared canvas, entirely in the browser.",[438,439,418],"tools","instagram","2026-11-25","\u002Fblog\u002Finstagram-carousel-padding-tool",{"title":443,"description":444,"tags":445,"postDate":451,"path":452,"url":420,"topic":427},"Getting Handy speech-to-text to type on NixOS and COSMIC, and to use my eGPU","Handy's shortcut did nothing, and after I fixed that, nothing got typed. A Wayland shortcut, a microphone, the paste method and an autostart file caused it, and the GPU did not.",[446,427,447,448,449,450],"troubleshooting","cosmic","wayland","speech-to-text","egpu","2026-11-19","\u002Fblog\u002Fhandy-speech-to-text-nixos-cosmic-egpu",{"title":454,"description":455,"tags":456,"postDate":460,"path":461,"url":420,"topic":427},"Getting a Razer Core X eGPU to work after login on NixOS, without timing the boot","My Razer Core X eGPU only worked if I timed it against boot. On NixOS the NVIDIA driver rejected the hotplugged card; PCI kernel parameters and a device node fixed it.",[446,427,450,457,458,459],"thunderbolt","nvidia","linux","2026-11-18","\u002Fblog\u002Frazer-core-x-egpu-hotplug-nixos",{"title":463,"description":464,"tags":465,"postDate":471,"path":472,"url":420,"topic":473},"Stop stashing half-finished work: use Git worktrees and Worktrunk","Git worktrees keep separate branches checked out at once. Worktrunk automates per-worktree setup. The same isolation also works for parallel AI agents.",[466,467,468,431,469,470],"git","worktrees","worktrunk","command line","workflow","2026-08-16","\u002Fblog\u002Fworktrees-with-worktrunk","command-line",{"title":475,"description":476,"tags":477,"postDate":481,"path":482,"url":420,"topic":480},"Self-Hosting my Git forge with Forgejo","Why I moved away from GitHub and chose a lightweight, community-driven alternative",[478,479,480,470],"homelab","open source","self-hosting","2026-04-29","\u002Fblog\u002Fself-hosting-my-git-forge",{"title":484,"description":485,"tags":486,"postDate":487,"path":488,"url":420,"topic":480},"Curating my own reading and discovery feed with RSS","Taking concrete steps away from algorithms using FreshRSS, self-hosted tools, and a pipeline built for me.",[478,479,480,470],"2026-02-08","\u002Fblog\u002Freading-and-discovery-feed-curation",{"title":490,"description":491,"tags":492,"postDate":494,"path":495,"url":420,"topic":480},"Fixing my broken Docker Immich+Traefik setup","Photo indexing failed in my Immich+Traefik setup. I'd misconfigured my Docker networking. Here's how I figured it out and what I changed.",[478,493],"networking","2025-10-31","\u002Fblog\u002Ffixing-docker-immich-traefik-setup",{"title":497,"description":498,"tags":499,"postDate":503,"path":504,"url":420,"topic":473},"Quickly outline large JSON responses with a custom jq function","Use jq to automatically map and visualize the structure of large JSON responses, perfect for exploring undocumented endpoints.",[500,501,469,502,431],"jq","json","automation","2025-10-19","\u002Fblog\u002Fjq-json-outline",{"title":506,"description":507,"tags":508,"postDate":512,"path":513,"url":420,"topic":480},"Why I added RSS feeds to my blog (and how I did it in Nuxt 3)","How I built RSS and Atom feed support for my Nuxt 3 website to let readers follow my content without social media algorithms.",[509,510,511],"nuxt","web development","tutorial","2025-08-31","\u002Fblog\u002Fsetting-up-rss-atom-feeds-nuxt3",1795692882169]